The v0.4.2 source tree and release archive do not redistribute any Character
Card v1/v2/v3 specification document. The v1/v2 repository did not declare a
license when verified. The v3 repository declares MIT, but its specification
is derived from the earlier v2 work; this project therefore applies the same
link-only policy to all external Character Card specifications instead of
making a downstream licensing determination. Earlier v0.4.0/v0.4.1 Git commits
remain historical records; no destructive history rewrite is implied by this
release.

RisuAI's GPL-3.0 source was reviewed only to identify de facto interoperability
extensions such as CHARX-JPEG, x_meta, and module.risum:

  https://github.com/kwaroran/Risuai/blob/c0ed1026de4b06a1c4600b79c789fea0616c297c/src/ts/characterCards.ts

MOMO Core does not include verbatim or mechanically translated RisuAI source
code. The CHARX adapter was nevertheless written after public implementation
sources had been reviewed, so this project does not describe that work as a
clean-room implementation. This provenance statement is not a legal conclusion
about derivative-work status; users and distributors must make their own
licensing assessment.

The downstream Character Foundry CHARX documentation was also reviewed as an
interoperability reference:

  https://github.com/character-foundry/character-foundry/blob/322fe8d940d1b91c978b43330b80ab2e115002e4/docs/charx.md

The verified Character Foundry commit did not contain a root LICENSE file, so
MOMO Core links to that document and does not redistribute it.

